sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Source and data traceability: 84/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "All seven sources carry DOIs (and PMIDs where they exist) in the docstring, the dataset README and paper_citations.bib; the upstream repository is pinned to commit 344863a with file:line references for the borrowed constants; the four fixtures are SHA-256 pinned and verified fail-closed at every run; the Horton & Hoyt fixture records DOI, PMID, formula and comparison range, and the formula is the one Horton & Hoyt published. Deductions: the Rule (2011) fixture's RMS beta error refers to a source-curve file (reports/source-curves/rule-2011-fig8-source-curves.json) that is not vendored, so the digitised Fig. 8 data behind the 0.154 figure cannot be traced from this repository (-6); the upstream Rust repository and the cited params.rs/planform.rs/presets.rs line numbers could not be independently resolved from the repository contents, so the alpha/beta provenance rests on assertion (-5); the paper-scale anchors cite only '2002 §1.1 / §4' without page or equation pinpoints (-3); Klüver (1966) is cited without page for the four-class taxonomy (-2). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L11–L44: Seven primary sources with DOI/PMID and the upstream commit hash and licence <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L11-L44>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L111–L138: FIXTURE_CHECKSUMS for four JSON inputs and RETINO_CONSTANT_PROVENANCE mapping each map constant to paper or upstream file:line <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L111-L138>; datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json L1–L15: Empirical anchor fixture with DOI, PMID, formula A/(E+E2), A = 17.3, E2 = 0.75 and comparison range <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json#L1-L15>; datasets/bressloff/README.md L9–L14: Fixture table with SHA-256, upstream path and description; Horton & Hoyt row marked as created in this repository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/datasets/bressloff/README.md#L9-L14>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.84"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Source and data traceability' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

